de la génération X. Les textes visent à démontrer que les baby-boomers sont des "complices et des parasites", au pire responsables de l'enfer néolibéral dans lequel peine dorénavent une société fermée aux jeunes et aux plus faibles. [Google Books] 6aÉvolution sociale94989 6aMondialismexAspect social939161 6aChangement social9397424 6920062aGénération du baby-boomzQuébec (Province) 6aQuébec (Province)xCivilisation966130 aRicard, Karen9391631 aDufour, Louise9391650 939167aBrûlé, Michel,d1964-  cLIVRE2ddc  bAmélie Gauthier01488nam a2200277 a 4500952012100000999001700121001000900138003000600147005001700153008004100170020001500211040001500226041000800241044000800249082001800257092001800275100003200293245003400325246001900359260004300378300002100421520067600442650004001118901003701158942001501195  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.RLEAd2011-02-16l0o813.54 G737pp001959451r2024-06-14 00:00:00w2011-03-26yLIVRE  c17153d1715343795201CaQJC20210302150245.0110216s2007||||xxu           000 f eng|c  a0399147195  aCaQJCbfre1 aeng  axxu0 a813.54bG737p  a813.54bG737p1 910919aGrafton, Sue,d1940-10aP is for peril /cSue Grafton03aP comme péril  aNew York :bG.P. Putnam's Sons,c2001.  a276 p. ;c22 cm.  aIt is now nine weeks since Dr Dowan Purcell vanished without trace. The sixty-nine-year-old doctor had said goodnight to his colleagues at the Pacific Meadows nursing home, had climbed into his car and driven away never to be seen again. His embittered first wife Fiona is convinced he is still alive. His second wife, Crystal a former stripper forty years his junior is just as sure he is dead. Enter private investigator Kinsey Malone, hired by Fiona to find out just what has happened to the man they loved. Enter also Tommy Hevener, an attractive flame-haired twenty-something who has set his romantic sights on Kinsey. And Tommy is a man with a very interesting past 694635aRoman américainy20e siècle  bStéfany-Cristina Ocampo-Brodeur  cLIVRE2ddc01132nam a2200253 a 4500952011600000999001700116001000900133003000600142005001700148008004100165020001500206040001500221041000800236044000700244082001500251092001500266100002700281245004400308260003100352300002100383520041400404650004500818942001500863  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2007-01-16l0o194 C576bp001778606r2023-05-31 00:00:00w2011-03-26yLIVRE  c17167d1716742772252CaQJC20180815114741.0070116s1979????fr ?????????? 0?? ? fre?d  a2070743829  aCaQJCbfre0 afre  afr0 a194bC576b  a194bC576b1 aBollon, Patrice93921910aCioran, l'hérétique /cPatrice Bollon  aParis :bGallimard,cc1997  a307 p. ;c21 cm.  aA la fois biographie et essai, ce livre soutient que non seulement il y a bien chez Cioran une pensée cohérente, sur la mystique, la politique et la conduite de l'existence, et que celle-ci est très loin d'être pessimiste ; mais qu'un fil d'Ariane traverse toute sa vie et lui confère son unité : déjouer toute certitude, penser sans cesse contre l'évidence rassurante, y compris contre soi. [Memento] 69213441aPhilosopheszFrancevBiographies  cLIVRE2ddc01537nam a2200445 i 38162110CaQJC20150705011443.0mt|                     970414s1993    qucŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒ 0ŒŒ Œ fre c       a2920174134  aCaQJCbfre0 afre  aquc0 a587.097bF616f0 a587.097bF616f2 aFleurbec (Organisation)9608710aFougères, prêles et lycopodes :bguide d'identification Fleurbec /cFleurbec ; dir. de la réd. et de l'éd. Gisèle Lamoureux  aSaint-Henri-de-Lévis :bGroupe Fleurbec.,c1993.  a511 p. :bill. en coul., cartes ;c19 cm0 aGuide d'identification Fleurbec.939253  aIndex: p. 481-511  aGlossaire: p. 453-462  a36.95 $ (1994)  aBibliogr.: p. 463-478 6aPtéridophyteszAmérique du Nord939254 6aPtéridophyteszQuébec (Province)939255 6aFougèreszAmérique du Nord939256 6aFougèreszQuébec (Province)939257 6aEquisetum939259 6aLycopodes939261 6939263aBotaniquev