hosomatique914009 698375aEsprit et corps 69298252aÉmotionsxAspect physiologique  cLIVRE2ddc02791nam a2200325 a   00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2010-08-06l1o005.7585 C562bp001926518r2023-05-30 00:00:00s2018-08-30w2011-03-26yLIVRE  c27475d2747543689657CaQJC20240508144944.0100806s1971????xxu?????????? 0?? ? eng?c  a9781590599433  aCaQJCbfre0 aeng  axxu0 a005.7585bC562b  a005.7585bC562b1 aChurcher, Clare95697110aBeginning SQL queries :bfrom novice to professional /cClare Churcher  aBerkeley, CA :bApress,cc2008.  axx, 218 p. :bill. ;c24 cm.  a36.95$  aIndex: p. 211-218.  aClare Churcher’s Beginning SQL Queries is your guide to mastering the lingua franca of the database industry: the SQL language. Good knowledge of SQL is crucial to anyone working with databases, because it is with SQL that you retrieve data, manipulate data, and generate business results. Knowing how to write good queries is the foundation for all work done in SQL, and it is a foundation that Clare lays well in her book.     Does not bore with syntax!     Helps you learn the underlying concepts involved in querying a database, and from there the syntax is easy     Provides exceptionally clear examples and explanations     Is academically sound while being practical and approachable What you’ll learn     Write simple queries to extract data from a single table     Understand relational algebra and calculus and why they are important     Combine data from many tables into one business result     Avoid pitfalls and traps such as Cartesian products and difficulties with null values     Summarize large amounts of data for reporting purposes     Apply set theory to the problems of manipulating data and generating reports Who this book is for Beginning SQL Queries is aimed at intelligent laypeople who need to extract information from a database, and at developers and other IT professionals who are new to SQL. The book is especially useful for business intelligence analysts who must ask more complex questions of their database than their GUI–based reporting software supports. Such people might be business owners wanting to target specific customers, scientists and students needing to extract subsets of their research data, or end users wanting to make the best use of databases for their clubs and societies. [AbeBooks] 6aProgrammation (Informatique)9525 6aBases de données relationnelles914315 6aSQL (Langage de programmation)956973 6939499aBases de donnéesxGestion  cLIVRE2ddc  bAmélie Gauthier01605nam a2200337 i   00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2005-07-03l3m1o306.89 C843gp001650400r2023-07-19 00:00:00s2015-02-12w2011-03-26yLIVRE  c27483d2748338199049CaQJC20181108124111.0mt|                     000920s2000    qucŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒ 0ŒŒ Œ fre c       a2890911772  aCaQJCbfre0 afre  aquc0 a306.89bC843g0 a306.89bC843g0 956995aCôté, Denyse,d1950-13aLa garde partagée :bl'équité en question /cDenyse Côté  aMontréal :bÉditions du Remue-ménage,c2000.  a202 p. ;c23 cm.0 aÀ vrai dire956997  aNotes (part. bibliogr.): p. 151-163  aBibliogr.: p. 165-174  aLes enfants de parents séparés devraient-ils être normalement élevés par leur père et leur mère ? Les mères qui refusent cette solution font-elles obstacle au sain développement de leur enfant ? La garde partagée devrait-elle être obligatoire ? Dans cet ouvrage, Denyse Côté démontre qu'il existe une marge entre le modèle et la réalité de la garde partagée, marge qu'il faut saisir pour s'assurer que les politiques en matière de garde n'instaurent de nouvelles modalités discriminatoires. [Memento] 6aGarde conjointe des enfants937461 6aRôle parental partagé (Divorce)99963 699959aEnfants de divorcés  cLIVRE2ddc01414nam a2200337 a   00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2009-08-27l0o155 T727ip001869874r2023-05-31 00:00:00w2011-03-26yLIVRE  c27521d2752143448006CaQJC2018052