mien95996712aL'Afrique sans dette /cDamien Millet  aLiège :bCADTM ;aParis :bSyllepse,cc2005.  a218 p. :bill. ;c22 cm.  aGlossaire: p. 211-214  aBibliogr. p. 215-218.  aPropose une analyse de l'histoire politico-économique de l'Afrique au XXe siècle, des causes de l'accroissement de la dette publique extérieure des différents états africains, de la politique d'ajustement structurel des organisations internationales, etc., ainsi qu'un plaidoyer pour une rupture avec la logique imposée par le FMI et la Banque mondiale. [Memento] 6aDettes extérieureszAfrique959968 6aAfriquexConditions économiquesy1960-921951  cLIVRE2ddc  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2007-04-17l2m1o336.34336 M653ap001765522r2023-07-26 00:00:00s2015-09-18w2011-03-26yLIVRE  c29395d29395  bJean-Christophe Desrosiers01249nam a2200325 i 38160583CaQJC20241205084416.0t|                     970204s1991    qucŒŒŒŒŒŒc    0ŒŒ Œ fre Œ       a2551127033  aCaOONLbfre0 afre  aquc0 a759.114074714471bP3770 a759.114074714471bP37703aLa Peinture au Québec, 1820-1850 :bnouveaux regards, nouvelles perspectives /csous la dir. de Mario Béland  aQuébec :bMusée du Québec. :bLes Publications du Québec.,cc1991.  a605 p. :bill. (certaines en coul) ;c31 cm  aIndex: p. 577-588  aCatalogue d'une exposition tenue au Musée du Québec du 16 octobre 1991 au 5 janvier 1992  aBibliogr.: p. 589-605 6aPeinture québécoise956343 6aPeinturey19e sièclezQuébec (Province)9599881 921315aBéland, Mario,d1953-2 91543aMusée du Québec  bAmélie C. Lepage  cLIVRE2ddc  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2005-07-03l0o759.114074714471 P377p01383126r2024-07-23 00:00:00w2011-03-26yLIVRE  c29411d2941103024nam a22003733a 43772004CaQJC20240508141029.0101216s2004????xxu??????????||??|?|eng??  a0321741765  a9780321741769  aCaQJCbfre0 aeng  axxu0 a005.133bH473c  a005.133bH473c1 aHejlsberg, Anders96001914aThe C# programming language /cAnders Hejlsberg ... et al. --  a4th ed.  aUpper Saddle River, NJ :bAddison-Wesley,cc2010.  axviii, 844 p. ;c24 cm.0 960020aMicrosoft .NET development series  a53.99$  aIndex: p. 815-844.  aLa couv. porte en outre: Special Annoted Edition for C# 4.0  a"Based on my own experience, I can safely say that every .NET developer who reads this will have at least one `aha' moment and will be a better developer for it."-From the Foreword by Don Box The popular C# programming language combines the high productivity of rapid application development languages with the raw power of C and C++. Updated to cover the new features of C# 4.0, including dynamic binding, named and optional parameters, and covariant and contravariant generic types, this release takes the language to the next level by adding the ability to cleanly write programs that don't rely on static type definitions. This allows dynamic programming languages such as Python, Ruby, and JavaScript to feel native to C#. The C# Programming Language, Fourth Edition, continues to be the authoritative and annotated technical reference for C# 4.0. Written by Anders Hejlsberg, the language's architect, and his colleagues, Mads Torgersen, Scott Wiltamuth, and Peter Golde, this volume has been completely updated for C# 4.0. The book provides the complete specification of the language, along with descriptions, reference materials, code samples, and annotations from twelve prominent C# gurus. The many annotations bring a depth and breadth of understanding rarely found in any programming book. As the main text of the book introduces the concepts of the C# language, cogent annotations explain why they are important, how they are used, how they relate to other languages, and even how they evolved. This book is the definitive, must-have reference for any developer who wants to understand C#. With annotations from: Brad Abrams, Joseph Albahari, Krzysztof Cwalina, Jesse Liberty, Eric Lippert, Christian Nagel, Vladimir Reshetnikov, Marek Safar, Chris Sells, Peter Sestoft, Jon Skeet, and Bill Wagner. [Memento] 6aC++ (Langage de programmation)93938191 aWiltamuth, Scott9600211 aGolde, Peter9600221 aTorgersen, Mads960023  cLIVRE2ddc  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2010-12-16l2o005.133 H473cp001955517r2023-05-30 00:00:00s2022-08-23w2011-03-26yLIVRE  c29431d29431  bJean-Christophe Desrosiers00909nam a2200301 a 450000100090000000300060000900500170001500800410003202000150007304000240008804100080011204400070012008200160012709200160014310000450015924500780020426000310028230000210031344000170033450400340035165000370038565000290042291200060045194200100045795201170046798000060058499900170059042868033CaQJC20160410010010.0070430s1998????fr ?????????? 0?? ? fre?c  a2012793061  aCaQMCLGbfredCaQJC0 afre  afr0 a303.3bJ86d  a303.3bJ86d0 aJouvenel, Bertrand de,d1903-198796005110aDu pouvoir :bhistoire naturelle de sa croissance /cBertrand de Jouvenel  aParis :bHachette,cc1998.  a607 p. ;c18 cm.0 aPluriel9473  aNotes bibliogr. au bas des p. 6aPouvoir (Sciences sociales)9973 69971aScience politiquee  mL  cLIVRE  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2007-04-30l0o303.3 J86dp001778185r2023-07-19 00:00:00w2011-03-26yLIVRE  a3  c29449d2944901304nam a2200349 a   00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2010-11-29l2m5o121 B624dp001952183r2023-05-30 00:00:00s2022-10-05w2011-03-26yLIVRE  c29467d2946743757576CaQJC20201015103445.0101129s1997????fr ?????????? 0?? ? fre?d  a9782082112406  aCaQJCbfre0 afre  afr0 a121bB624d  a121bB624d1 aBitbol, Michel,d1954-96008510aDe l'intérieur du monde :bpour une philosophie et une science des relations /cMichel Bitbol  aParis :bFlammarion,c2010.  a719 p. ;c24 cm.3 aLa Bibliothèque des savoirs960087  a59.95$  aIndex: p. 709-716.  aBibliogr.: p. 685-707.  aNotes (part. bibliogr.) au bas de certaines p.  