COLD...an unforgetable novel of revenge, conspiracy, and murder that brings a band of unlikely heroes face-to-face with their greatest threat.  Oliver Stone, the leader of the mysterious group that calls itself the Camel Club, is both feared and respected by those who've crossed his path. Keeping a vigilant watch over our leaders in Washington, D.C., the Camel Club has won over some allies, but it has also earned formidable enemies-including those in power who will do anything to prevent Stone and his friends from uncovering the hidden, secret work of the government.  Annabelle Conroy, an honorary member of the Camel Club, is also the greatest con artist of her generation. She has swindled forty million dollars from casino king Jerry Bagger, the man who murdered her mother. Now he's hot on her trail with only one goal in mind: Annabelle's death. But as Stone and the Camel Club circle the wagons to protect Annabelle, a new opponent, who makes Bagger's menace pale by comparison, suddenly arises.  One by one, men from Stone's shadowy past are turning up dead. Behind this slaughter stands one man: Harry Finn. To almost all who know him, Finn is a doting father and loving husband who uses his skills behind the scenes to keep our nation safe. But the other face of Harry Finn is that of an unstoppable killer who inevitably sets his lethal bull's-eye on Oliver Stone. And with Finn, Stone may well have met his match. [AbeBooks] 6945940aRomans américains  bStéfany-Cristina Ocampo-Brodeur  cLIVRE2ddc00948nam a2200289 i 450000100090000000300060000900500170001500800490003204000230008104100080010404400070011208200190011909200190013824500850015725000290024226000290027130000210030044000270032165000330034865000440038165000440042570000370046994200100050695201190051698000060063599900170064138124183CaQJC20150415165116.0861030s1985    fr ****ŒŒŒŒŒŒ 0Œ* Œ fre d  aCaQMCDbfrecCaQJC0 afre  afr0 a841.008bP745b  a841.008bP745b03aLa Poésie baroque et précieuse, (1550-1650) /c[choix de] André Blanchard. --  aNouv. éd. rev. et augm.  aParis :bSeghers,c1985.  a357 p. ;c19 cm. 0aCollection P.S.965033 6aLittérature baroque.965035 6aPoésie françaisey16e siècle.965037 6aPoésie françaisey17e siècle.9401551 965038aBlanchard, André,d1906-  cLIVRE  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2005-07-03l0o841.008 P745bp01171244r2024-08-06 00:00:00w2011-03-26yLIVRE  a3  c32797d3279701829nam a2200337 i   00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2005-07-03l3m3o553.7 B758bp001732799r2024-06-19 00:00:00s2016-02-18w2011-03-26yLIVRE  c32837d3283738290254CaQJC20240124142528.0mt|                     031208s2003    qucŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒ 0ŒŒ Œ fre c       a2921561921  aCaQJCbfre0 afre  aquc0 a553.7bB758b0 a553.7bB758b0 aBouguerra, Mohamed Larbi,d1936-96509514aLes batailles de l'eau :bpour un bien commun de l'humanité /cMohamed Larbi Bouguerra  aMontréal :bÉcosociété,c2003.  a239 p. ;c20 cm0 aEnjeux planète ;v795379  aNotes: p. 225-239  aBibliogr.: p. 223-224  aL’eau n’est pas seulement une ressource économique dont le traitement offre un formidable marché aux multinationales. Cet ouvrage montre que l’usage de l’eau est révélateur de notre rapport à la planète, à son devenir et aux biens communs de l’humanité. Deux milliards de personnes n’ont pas accès à l’eau courante. Le partage de l’eau est devenu un enjeu stratégique. Conférences internationales, forums, projets de loi se succèdent à un rythme soutenu. Cet ouvrage veut d’abord être une contribution au débat fondée sur des faits, des données scientifiques, des chiffres, des expériences et des luttes locales, et apporter, ensuite, un éclairage au lecteur pour qu’il puisse se déterminer dans des discussions actuelles. [Écosociété] 6aEauxApprovisionnement9391591 6920057aEau  cLIVRE2ddc  bAmélie Gauthier01165nam a2200361 i 38203720CaQJC20151016112748.0t|                     010404s1996    fr ŒŒŒŒ