tomical charts /cAnatomical Chart Company, Wolters Kluwer Health/Lippincott Williams & Wilkins.13aDiseases and disorders  aSkokie, IL :bWolters Kluwer Health/Lippincott Williams & Wilkins,c2008.  a83 p. de pl. :bill. en coul. ;c31 cm  aThe 3rd Edition of Diseases and Disorders: The World's Best Anatomical Charts features 70 new and updated anatomical charts created by some of the world's best medical illustrators. These anatomical charts show the human body in a format that provides a clear and visual understanding of the most important diseases and disorders. Medical terminology and easy to understand supporting text is always printed directly on each chart so you never have to refer to a separate key card or manual." "All of our anatomical charts are printed in vivid, lifelike colors on high-quality paper, and bound together in a spiral notebook. With its convenient size and spiral bound format, this book is ideal for studying diseases and disorders of the human body, patient consultation, or quick reference. 6aAnatomie humaine94371 6aAtlas92963322 aAnatomical Chart Company91088112 aWolters Kluwer Health/Lippincott Williams & Wilkin9108812  bAmélie Arseneault  2ddccLIVRE  c65843d6584301739nam a2200373 i   00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.RLEAd2005-07-03g19.00l1o823.8 D754hp01374973r2024-06-14 00:00:00s2018-06-20yLIVRE  c65887d6588738159256CaQJC20240625153950.0ta961202s1996    fr ŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒ 0ŒŒ f eng c       a2070394581  aCaQJCbfredCaQJCerda1 afreaeng  afr0 a823.8bD754h0 942113aDoyle, Arthur Conan,cSir,d1859-193012aL'homme à la lèvre tordue et autres aventures de Sherlock Holmes =bThe man with the twisted lips and other adventures of Sherlock Holmes /cSir Arthur Conan Doyle ; trad. de l'anglais par Julie Pujos en collab avec Marie-Pierre Coutelle 1aParis :bGallimard,c1996.  a285 p, 16 p. de pl. :bill. ;c18 cm  2rdacontentatextebtxt  2rdamediaasans médiationbn  2rdacarrieravolumebnc  a19.95$ (1996)  aUne jeune fille un peu sotte dont le mystérieux fiancé a disparu le jour du mariage ; un homme respectable, assassiné par un affreux infirme à la lèvre tordue ; un roi imprudent qui redoute un ravissant maître-chanteur ; un ingénieur hydraulique à qui il manque un pouce : tels sont les clients du célèbre détective Holmes...  aTexte en anglais et trad. française en regard. 6aHolmes, Sherlock (Personnage fictif)934963 691137aRoman anglaisy20e siècle 69575aRoman policier1 aFolio bilingue 0922263aFolio bilingue  bStéphanie Tellier  cLIVRE00961nam a22002892a 450000100090000000300060000900500170001500800520003204100080008404400070009208200200009909200200011909200190013910000360015824500800019426000310027430000310030544000290033650400270036565100610039265100600045391200060051394200100051995201190052998000060064899900170065438270861CaQJC20160428120940.0020915s1966    fr ŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒ 0ŒŒ Œ fre0 afre  afr0 a914.2073bP259v  a914.2073bP259v  a942.073bP259v0 aParreaux, André,d1906-95524313aLa vie quotidienne en Angleterre au temps de Georges III /cAndré Parreaux  aParis :bHachette,cc1966.  a287 p. :bcarte. ;c20 cm.0 aLa Vie quotidienne93781  aBibliogr.: p. 275-277. 6aGrande-BretagnexConditions socialesy18e siècle955247 6955249aGrande-BretagnexMoeurs et coutumesy18e siècle  mL  cLIVRE  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2010-11-09l0o942.073 P259vp01948181r2025-01-09 00:00:00w2011-03-26yLIVRE  a3  c65899d6589900922nam a2200277 a 450000100090000000300060000900500170001500800400003202000150007204000150008704100080010204400070011008200180011709200180013510000310015324500920018426000380027630000210031444000160033553400660035165000400041790100210045794200150047895201340049399900170062743360156CaQJC20240221084739.0040204s2003    fr ||||       000|f fre   a2070304787  aCaQJCbfre0 afre  afr0 a813.54bR845j  a813.54bR845j  aRoth, Philip,d1933-962