According to Philip Kotler, the widely acknowledged "father" ofmodern marketing, and Fernando Trias de Bes the marketingtechniques pioneered in the 1960s and '70s have worked too well.Fierce competition among products with little or nothing todistinguish one from another, along with modern product positioningand targeted marketing techniques, have led to increasing marketsegmentation. If the trend continues, individual market segmentssoon will be too small to be profitable. In Lateral Marketing,Kotler and Trias de Bes unveil a revolutionary new model to helpreaders expand beyond vertical segmentation and generate freshmarketing ideas and opportunities.
Philip Kotler (Chicago, IL) is the S. C. Johnson & SonDistinguished Professor of International Marketing at NorthwesternUniversity's Kellogg School of Management. Fernando Trias de Bes(Barcelona, Spain) is the founder of Salvetti & Llombart whoseclients include Pepsico, Sony, Hewlett-Packard, Nestlé, CreditSuisse, and other top corporations. [AbeBooks] 6aMarketingxGestion.972011 aTrias de Bes, Fernando9124131  cLIVRE2ddc01198nam a2200361 i   00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2005-07-03l1o320.54 D559np001617444r2023-07-26 00:00:00s2017-12-13w2011-03-26yLIVRE  c79295d7929538205270CaQJC20181113155200.0mt|                     010312s2000    fr ŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒ 0ŒŒ Œ fre d       a2080674943  a(CaQMCD)A015108  aCaQMCDbfre0 afre  afr0 a320.54bD559n0 a320.54bD559n1 aDieckhoff, Alain912419313aLa nation dans tous ses États :bles identités nationales en mouvement /cAlain Dieckhoff  aParis :bFlammarion,cc2000.  a354 p. ;c21 cm0 92796aEssais  aIndex: p. 341-351  aNotes (part. bibliogr.): p. 311-339  aL'auteur analyse le nationalisme actuel et insiste sur la nécessité de la réforme de l'Etat-nation. [Memento]26aNationalisme9794 6aÉtat9975 6aModernité94993 6aDémocratie97631  cLIVRE2ddc01145nam a2200361 i 38203571CaQJC20150819010408.0mt|                     971215s1996    fr ŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒ 0ŒŒ Œ fre c       a2070533506  aCaQJCbfre0 afre  afr0 a939.43bM443a0 a939.43bM443a0 aMatthiae, Paolo,d1940-912420010aAux origines de la Syrie :bEbla retrouvée /cPaolo Matthiae ; trad. de Françoise Liffran18aEbla retrouvée  aParis :bGallimard,cc1996.  a160 p. :bill. (certaines en coul.), cartes ;c18 cm0 928663aDécouvertes Gallimard.pArchéologie.v276  aIndex : p. 156-159  aBibliogr. : p. 152 6aEbla (Ville ancienne)9124203 69111737aSyriexAntiquités0 aEbla retrouvée  mL  cLIVRE  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2005-07-03l0o939.43 M443ap001658076r2025-