tros formatos). Material indispensable para reforzar problemas especificos que los alumnos tengan con alguna destreza en particular. Cada unidad tiene unos objetivos comunicativos, gramaticales y lexicos que se trabajan a lo largo de seis paginas, a traves de documentos autenticos que sirven para contextualizar la practica posterior de la destreza correspondiente. [AbeBooks] 6aEspagnol (Langue)vVocabulaires et manuels de conversation921138 692432aEspagnol (Langue)vManuels pour allophones  cLIVRE2ddc  bAmélie C. Lepage01969nam a2200337 i   00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2005-07-03l0o302.17 G549cp001735161r2023-07-13 00:00:00w2011-03-26yLIVRE  c107689d10768938291878CaQJC20181030170018.0mt|                     040225s1999    xxuŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒ 0ŒŒ Œ eng c       a0465014909  aCaQJCbfre0 aeng  axxu0 a302.17bG549c0 a302.17bG549c1 aGlassner, Barry915289214aThe culture of fear :bwhy Americans are afraid of the wrong things /cBarry Glassner  aNew York :bBasic Books,c1999.  axxviii, 282 p. ;c21 cm  aIndex: p. 265-282  aNotes (part. bibliogr.): p. 211-257  aIn the age of 9/11, the Iraq War, financial collapse, and Amber Alerts, our society is defined by fear. So it's not surprising that three out of four Americans say they feel more fearful today then they did twenty years ago. But are we living in exceptionally dangerous times? In The Culture of Fear, sociologist Barry Glassner demonstrates that it is our perception of danger that has increased, not the actual level of risk. Glassner exposes the people and organizations that manipulate our perceptions and profit from our fears, including advocacy groups that raise money by exaggerating the prevalence of particular diseases and politicians who win elections by heightening concerns about crime, drug use, and terrorism. In this new edition of a classic book—more relevant now than when it was first published—Glassner exposes the price we pay for social panic. [Amazon] 6aPeurzÉtats-Unis9152893 6aPerception socialezÉtats-Unis9152894 6aProblèmes sociauxzÉtats-Unis9152895 6aAngoissezÉtats-Unis9152896  cLIVRE2ddc01245nam a2200289 a 450000100090000000300060000900500170001500800410003202000150007304000150008804100080010304400070011108200210011809200210013910000360016024500850019626000350028130000480031650000260036450400230039052003800041365000590079365000470085294200150089999900190091490100220093343419434CaQJC20250128152958.0090622|||||||||fr     |||||||||||||fre||  a2743007362  aCaQJCbfre0 afre  afr0 a621.38153bD778t  a621.38153bD778t1 aDreyfus-Alain, Bertrand915290400aTechnologie en microélectronique à câblage imprimé /cBertrand Dreyfus-Alain  aParis :bÉd. Tec & doc,c2005  axviii, 482, 1 p. :btabl., graph. ;c25 cm.  aGlossaire: p. 481-482  aBibliogr.: p. 483.  aMontage, assemblage et lavage des microcircuits. L'ouvrage fait le point sur les avancées théoriques, ainsi que sur l'outillage et les équipements employés. Les composants, les circuits électriques, l'implantation et le routage, les encres à braser, l'alliage de brasure tendre à base d'étain ou la protection des surfaces contre la corrosion sont décrits. [Memento] 6aCircuits imprimésxConception et construction9152905 6aMontage en surface (Électronique)9152907  cLIVRE2ddc  c107693d107693  bAmélie C. Lepage00839nam a2200277 i 450000100090000000300060000900500170001500700030003200800530003504000150008804100080010304400070011108200170011809200170013510000620015224500480021426000320026230000210029444000400031565000270035591200110038294200100039395201330040398000060053699900190054238181444CaQJC20190227121657.0t|990317s1967    fr ŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒŒ 0ŒŒ e fre c  aCaQJCbfre0 afre  afr0 a844.9bL462e  a844.9bL462e1 aLe Clézio, J. M. G.q(Jean Marie Gustave),d1940-92107512aL'extase matérielle /cJ. M. G. Le Clézio  aParis :bGallimard,cc1967.  a313 p. ;c17 cm. 0aIdées ;pLittérature.