. ; trad. de l'allemand par C. Bastyns...et al.13aLa querelle allemande des sciences  sociales.0 aParis :bÉditions Complexe,c1979.  a278 p. ;c23 cm.0 aTextes  aNotes (part. bibliogr.): p. 249-275.  aBibliogr.: p. 277-278.  aChoix de douze textes importants présentant la pensée allemande sur le positivisme dans les sciences sociales. [SDM]  pTitre original :tDer Positivismusstreit in der deutschen Soziologie. 6aSociologie9348967 6aPositivisme9346471 aAdorno, Theodor W.,d1903-19699393812 0aTextes (Complexe (Firme))969967  bAnnabel Labelle  cLIVRE2ddc  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2001-07-08g36.00l0o301 D278p001979969r2023-07-13 00:00:00w2011-07-08yLIVRE  c158177d15817702267cam a2200397 a CaQMUb10763021CaQMU20250424124354.0ta791116s1979    fr ||||| b    00| | fre d  a2228124508qv.1  a2228126403qv.2  aCaQJCbfre  afre  afr  a300bF765m1 9182895aFougeyrollas, Pierre,d1922-200810aSavoirs et idéologie dans les sciences sociales /cPierre Fougeyrollas.00aParis :bPayot,c1979.  a2 v. ;c23 cm.1 aBibliothèque scientifique  aNotes (part. bibliogr.) au bas des p.  tVol.1 Sciences sociales et marxisme. -- v.2 Les processus sociaux contemporains.  aL'homme (en société) est libre, pourtant il est dans les fers (de l'action collective). Raymond Boudon renouvelle à sa manière le paradoxe de J.J. Rousseau en développant une analyse sociologique dont les sujets sont à la fois libres et conscients de leurs actes individuels et inconscients des effets collectifs que provoque leur agrégation. Cette idée fondamentale qu'il a déjà brillamment illustrée dans d'autres ouvrages, Raymond Boudon la reprend ici dans la perspective d'une introduction à l'analyse sociologique. La logique du social est un livre important qui permet à l'auteur de faire la théorie de sa pratique tout en la rattachant aux grands sociologues du passé (Tocqueville, Marx, Durkheim, Max Weber...) et de battre en brèche le sociologisme et ses diverses variantes. [Google Books] 6925167aSocialisme 6aSciences sociales98021 6aCommunisme et sciences sociales9196906 6aMouvements sociauxy20e sièclexHistoire  aSciences sociales et marxisme.4 aLes processus sociaux contemporains.  aBibliothèque scientifique913551  bAnnabel Labelle  cLIVRE2ddc  00102ddc4070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2001-07-08hv.1l0o300 F765mp001980009r2023-07-13 00:00:00w2011-07-08yLIVRE  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2001-07-08hv.2l0o300 F765mp001980059r2023-07-13 00:00:00w2011-07-08yLIVRE  c158181d15818101442cam a2200337 a CaQMUb10753709CaQMU20240916143719.0ta790109m1978    fr ||||| b   i001 | fre d  a9232010135qUnesco  a2719308091qMouton  aCaQJCbfre  afre  afr  a300bH387t00aTendances principales de la recherche dans les sciences sociales et humaines /csous la dir. de Jacques Havet ; préf. de Amadou-Mathar M'Bow et de René Maheu.00aParis :bMouton,cc1978.  a2 v. ;c25 cm.  a"Cet ouvrage est le résultat d'une étude commencée par l'Unesco en 1965".  aComprend des références bibliogr..1 t1re ptie. Sciences sociales.--2e ptie. v.1 Sciences anthropologiques et historiques ; Esthétique et sciences de l'art.--2e ptie. v.2 Science juridique ; Philosophie.269176775aUnesco 6aSciences socialesxRecherche921687 6aSciences humainesxRecherche9516151 aHavet, Jacques9196907  bAmélie Gauthier  cLIVRE2ddc  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2001-07-08hv.1l0o300 H387t ptie 2p001980106r2023-07-13 00:00:00yLIVRE  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2001-07-08hv.2l0o300 H387t ptie 2p001980156r2023-07-13 00:00:00w2011-07-08yLIVRE  c158183d15818302354cam a2200265 a 4500952012400000999001900124001000900143003000600152005001700158008004100175020001600216040002000232041000800252082001500260100003100275245010400306260004100410300002900451500002300480504003400503520146800537650003502005650003302040942001502073  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2011-07-11g184.95l0o664 C889fp001965350r2024-07-19 00:00:00w2011-07-11yLIVRE  c158191d15819114281936CaQJC20190531160340.0060301s2006    flua     b    001 0 eng    a0849341973   aDLCdCaQJCbfre0 aeng0 a664bC889f1 aCramer, Michael M.919691010aFood plant sanitation :bdesign, maintenance, and good manufacturing practices /cMichael M. Cramer  aBoca Raton, FL :bCRC Press,cc2006.  a283 p. :bill. ;c24 cm.  aIndex: p. 265-283.  aBibliogr. à la fin des chap.  aPrevention of food borne illnesses, reduction of product spoilage, and improvements to product quality are ongoing concerns in the food manufacturing industry. Providing broad but practical information, Food Plant Sanitation: Design, Maintenance, and Good Manufacturing Practices shows how to effectively remove soil and microorganisms from the processing environment to prevent unhygienic manufacturing conditions.

Using photographs, diagrams, and tables, this reference offers solutions to effective food sanitation. The book begins with discussions on the regulatory requirements of food plant sanitation and the identification of microorganisms of food manufacturing concern. Later chapters explore the principles of sanitary design, the use of proven sanitation techniques, and the means of verifying sanitation, such as adenosine triphosphate (ATP). The final chapters identify sanitary practices for plant personnel and visitors, provide a comprehensive pest management plan, and offer strategies for preventing chemical and physical food safety hazards.

Drawing on almost 30 years of industry experience, the author gives real-world examples and practical, up-to-date information. These features, combined with a direct, easy-to-read format, demonstrate how you can use the techniques presented for implementation and training purposes, making this reference ideal for food safety and quality personnel as well as plant managers and designers. [Memento] 6aIndustrie alimentaire 9196791 6965755aHygiène industrielle  2ddccLIVRE00976nam a2200265 a 4500952014300000999001900143001001000162003000600172005001700178008004100195020001500236040002900251041000800280082001900288245009400307260007400401300003400475500002300509504003400532650004400566650003300610700002700643700002500670942001500695  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2011-07-11g198.95l5m4o664.0282 P963p001965392r2024-07-19 00:00:00s2023-03-20w2011-07-11yLIVRE  c158193d158193001114634CaQJC20190429121504.0910326s1991||||nyua   | b    001 | eng    a0442302827  aUtOrBLWcDLCdCaQJcbfre0 aeng0 a664.0282bP96300aProcessing and packaging of heat preserved foods /cedited by J.A.G. Rees and J. Bettison  aNew York, N.Y. :bVan Nostrand Reinhold ;aGlasgow :bBlackie,c1991.  axiii, 250 p. :bill ;c25 cm.  aIndex: p. 247-250.  aBibliogr. à la fin des chap. 6aConservation et mise en conserves97953 6aConservesxIndustrie91493211 aRees, J. A. G.91969111 aBettison, J.9196909  2ddccLIVRE02031cam a22003014a 4500952012700000999001900127001001000146003000600156005001700162008004100179020001900220040002000239041000800259082001800267245010200285260004200387300003300429490002100462500002300483504003400506520101300540650002401553650004201577650002901619700003001648700003601678942001501714  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2011-07-11g242.00l0o641.373 W569p001964907r2024-07-18 00:00:00w2011-07-11yLIVRE  c158195d158195002731005CaQJC20190429143945.0080219s2008    iaua     b    001 0 eng    a9780813809038   aDLCdCaQJCbfre0 aeng0 a641.373bW56900aWhey processing, functionality and health benefits /ceditors, Charles I. Onwulata, Peter J. Huth  aAmes, Iowa :bWiley-Blackwell,c2008.  axiv, 400 p. :bill ;c24 cm.1 aIFT Press series  aIndex: p. 393-400.  aBibliogr. à la fin des chap.  aWhey Processing, Functionality and Health Benefits provides a review of the current state of the science related to novel processes, functionality, and health benefit implications and documents the biological role of whey protein in selected areas that include muscle metabolism after exercise, muscle and body composition in the elderly, weight management, food intake regulation, and maintenance of bone mass. The topics addressed and the subject experts represent the best science knowledge base in these areas. In some of these areas, the state of the art and science are compelling, and emerging data are confirming and solidifying the human knowledge base. Collating the understanding and knowledge of the metabolic roles of whey protein and developing the clinical datasets that demonstrate efficacy for improving human health will speed up new product innovations and sustainable opportunities for the food industry as evidenced by the processing and functionality research conducted so far. [Amazon] 0aLactosérum9196914 0aProduits laitiers9133229xTraitement 0aProduits laitiers9358211 aOnwulata, Charles91969121 aHuth, Peterq(Peter J.)9196913  2ddccLIVRE01245nam a2200289 a 4500001001000000003000600010005001700016008004100033020001500074040002900089041000800118082001600126245022200142260010400364300003300468500002300501504003400524650004300558700002300601700002600624710003600650711007300686942001500759952014000774999001900914901002200933000191769CaQJC20250117093042.0840309s1982    enka     b    101 0 eng    a0853341435  aUtOrBLWcDLCdCaQJCbfre0 aeng00a641.3bF68600aFood proteins :bproceedings of the Kellogg Foundation International Symposium