La dépression masculine :bcomprendre et faire face /cThéodore Hovaguimian en collaboration avec Philippe Barraud.  aChêne-Bourg :bMédecine & hygiène,c2013, c2012.  a109 p. ;c17 cm.  aBibliogr.: p. 105-109.  aCette étude sur la dépression masculine montre qu'il s'agit d'un concept récent et comment elle diffère de la dépression féminine. Elle décrit les événements qui peuvent conduire à une dépression, sa mécanique, les soins par les médicaments ou la psychothérapie, l'accompagnement de l'homme déprimé et aborde enfin le suicide et la prévention de la rechute. [Memento] 6aDépression chez l'homme92088481 aBarraud, Philippe,d1949-  aYLB (09-12-13)  2ddccLIVRE02311cam a2200385 a 0003795211CaQJC20230510113358.0090123s2009    nyuab           0 f eng  a9781416971733  aDLCdCaQJCbfreerda0 aeng  anyu0 a813.54bW526L1 aWesterfeld, Scott,d1963-929531010aLeviathan /cwritten by Scott Westerfeld ; illustrated by Keith Thompson.03aLéviathan 1aNew York :bSimon Pulse,c2009.  a440 p. :bill., cartes ;c24 cm.  2rdacontentatextebtxt  2rdamediaasans médiationbn  2rdacarrieravolumebnc1 aLeviathan trilogy   aTrilogie de la série Léviathan (Léviathan, Béhémoth, Goliath)  aIt is the cusp of World War I, and all the European powers are arming up. The Austro-Hungarians and Germans have their Clankers, steam-driven iron machines loaded with guns and ammunition. The British Darwinists employ fabricated animals as their weaponry. Their Leviathan is a whale airship, and the most masterful beast in the British fleet.  Aleksandar Ferdinand, prince of the Austro-Hungarian Empire, is on the run. His own people have turned on him. His title is worthless. All he has is a battle-torn Stormwalker and a loyal crew of men.  Deryn Sharp is a commoner, a girl disguised as a boy in the British Air Service. She's a brilliant airman. But her secret is in constant danger of being discovered.  With the Great War brewing, Alek's and Deryn's paths cross in the most unexpected way...taking them both aboard the Leviathan on a fantastical, around-the-world adventure. One that will change both their lives forever. [Amazon] 69214451aRoman américainy21e siècle 69260861aPrincesvRomans, nouvelles, etc.  69340102aGénie génétiquevRomans, nouvelles, etc.  69141995aGuerre vRomans, nouvelles, etc1 9260871aThompson, Keith,d1982- 0aLeviathan trilogy ;9360598v1  bAndréanne Sauvé  cLIVRE  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.RLEAd2014-01-06g23.37l1o813.54 W526Lp002070996r2024-06-14 00:00:00s2014-01-24v22.99yLIVRE  c309461d30946101397nam a2200301 a 4500952013500000999001900135001001100154003000600165005001700171008004100188020001800229040002000247041000800267082001700275100003800292245009000330260004000420300002100460440002000481440002700501500010800528520027900636546007100915650004000986700001801026901003601044942001501080  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.RLEAd2014-01-06g11.13l0o818.5  C594tp002070970r2024-06-14 00:00:00v10.95w2014-01-06yLIVRE  c309471d3094710000702977CaQJC20241119082824.0021101s2002    fr            000   eng    a9782253086918  aSDMbfredCaQJC0 aeng0 a818.5bC594t1 aClark, Mary Higginsd1931-91716910aTerror stalks the class reunion /cMary Higgins Clark ; annotations par Henri Yvinec.  aParis :bLe Livre de poche,cc2002.  a160 p. ;c17 cm. 0aLire en anglais 3aLe Livre de poche9479  a"Cette nouvelle est extraite du recueil The Anastasia syndrome and other stories"--Verso de la p. de t.  aLovely young Kay Crandall has come back for the reunion of a high school where she once taught. But Kay cannot guess that the happy occasion is about to turn into a nightmare -- as she falls into the hands of a madman who wants to make her into his wife -- and his victim...  aTexte en anglais avec exercices en français à la fin des textes. 694635aRoman américainy20e siècle1 aYvinec, Henri  aAL (21-01-14)bAmélie Gauthier  2ddccLIVRE01499nam a2200277 a 4500952015000000999001900150003000600169005001700175008004100192020001800233040001500251041000800266044000800274082001800282100003600300245004200336260003200378300002100410500006700431500005200498505023500550520036100785650002301146901003701169942001501206  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.RLEAd2014-01-06g11.17l2m1o828.9  D131sp002070954r2024-06-14 00:00:00s2014-05-08v10.99w2014-01-06yLIVRE  c309481d309481CaQJC20221011143257.0140121t2010    xxu||||| |||| 00| 0 eng d  a9780141310343  aCaQJCbfre0 aeng  axxu0 a823.9 bD131f1 aDahl, Roald,d1916-19909121239  aSkin and other stories /cRoald Dahl.  aNew York :  bSpeak,c2010.  a212 p. ;c22 cm.  aIntroduces teenagers to the adult short stories of Roald Dahl.  aOriginally published: New York : Viking, c2000.  aDépouillement :  Skin -- Lamb to the slaughter -- The sound machine -- An African story -- Galloping Foxley -- The wish -- The surgeon -- Dip in the pool -- The champion of the world -- Beware of the dog -- My lady love, my dove.  aHow would you get rid of a murder weapon without causing suspicion? Where would you hide a diamond where no one else would think of looking? What if you found out that the tattoo on your back was worth over a million dollars? You will discover that just about anything is possible in a Roald Dahl story, and here are eleven of his very best. [AbeBooks.com] 69641aRoman anglais  aAL (21-01-14)bÉlaine Bélanger  cLIVRE2ddc01460nam a2200265 a 4500952013400000999001900134003000600153005001700159008004100176020001800217040001500235041000800250044000700258082001800265100003600283245008200319246002500401260004400426490003000470520059200500650002301092830002701115901003701142942001501179  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.RLEAd2014-02-20g11.17l0o823.9 D131up002075572r2024-06-14 00:00:00v10.99w2014-02-20yLIVRE  c309491d309491CaQJC20221011143258.0140220t2013    fr ||||| |||| 00| 0 eng d  a9782253061366  aCaQJCbfre0 aeng  afr0 a823.9 bD131u1 aDahl, Roald,d1916-1990912123904aThe umbrella man and other stories /cchoix et annotations par Daniel Yvinec.03aL'homme au parapluie  aParis:bLe Livre de poche,c2013, 1992.1 aLe livre de pochev; 8670  aUn " gentleman " anglais bien étrange..., un auto-stoppeur sans-gêne..., une enfant à jamais blessée par un " remariage "..., un géant repenti..., une vieille dame mystérieuse au milieu des bois, en compagnie de ses six (ou sept) chats... Tels sont, entre autres, les personnages qui peuplent ces nouvelles anglaises et américaines contemporaines, mélanges d'humour, de poésie, d'humanité, d'excentricité, dans la plus pure tradition anglo-saxonne. Textes authentiques, non simplifiés, non abrégés, d'auteurs prestigieux, écrits dans une langue très accessible. [Decitre] 69641aRoman anglais 3aLe Livre de poche9479  aAL (20-02-14)bÉlaine Bélanger  cLIVRE2ddc01450nam a2200277 a 4500952013300000999001900133003000600152005001700158008004100175020001800216040001500234041000800249044000800257082001800265100003600283245006900319246002800388246003000416260004700446300003100493520055300524650002301077700002001100901003701120942001501157  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.RLEAd2014-01-10g8.12l0o823.9  D131jp002070988r2024-06-14 00:00:00v7.99w2014-01-10yLIVRE  c309501d309501CaQJC20221011143257.0140121t2013    xxu||||| |||| 00| 0 eng d  a9780142410363  aCaQJCbfre0 aeng  axxu0 a823.9 bD131j1 aDahl, Roald,d1916-19909121239  aJames and the giant peach /cRoald Dahl ; ill. by Quentin Blake.13aJames & the giant peach03aJames et la grosse pêche  aNew York :  bPuffin Books,c2013, ©1975.  a146 p. :b ill. ; c20 cm.  aAfter James Henry Trotter's parents are tragically eaten by a rhinoceros, he goes to live with his two horrible aunts, Spiker and Sponge. Life there is no fun, until James accidentally drops some magic crystals by the old peach tree and strange things start to happen. The peach at the top of the tree begins to grow, and before long it's as big as a house. Inside, James meets a bunch of oversized friends-Grasshopper, Centipede, Ladybug, and more. With a snip of the stem, the peach starts rolling away, and the great adventure begins! [AbeBooks] 69641aRoman anglais1 aBlake, Quentin   aAL (21-01-14)bÉlaine Bélanger  cLIVRE2ddc01321nam a2200265 a 4500952014800000999001900148003000600167005001700173008004100190020001800231040001500249041000800264044000800272082001800280100003600298245006100334246003100395260004700426300003000473520045700503650002300960700002000983901003701003942001501040  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.RLEAd2013-12-17g8.12l1m2o823.9  D131fp002070441r2024-06-14 00:00:00s2019-05-10v7.99w2013-12-17yLIVRE  c309511d309511CaQJC20221011143257.0140121t2007    xxu||||| |||| 00| 0 eng d  a9780142410349  aCaQJCbfre0 aeng  axxu0 a823.9 bD131f1 aDahl, Roald,d1916-19909121239  aFantastic Mr. Fox /cRoald Dahl ; ill. by Quentin Blake.03aFantastique Maître Renard  aNew York :  bPuffin Books,c2007, ©1970.  a81 p. :b ill. ; c20 cm.  aSomeone's been stealing from the three meanest farmers around, and they know the identity of the thief-it's Fantastic Mr. Fox! Working alone they could never catch him; but now fat Boggis, squat Bunce, and skinny Bean have joined forces, and they have Mr. Fox and his family surrounded. What they don't know is that they're not dealing with just any fox-Mr. Fox would rather die than surrender. Only the most fantastic plan can save him now. [AbeBooks] 69641aRoman anglais1 aBlake, Quentin   aAL (21-01-14)bÉlaine Bélanger  cLIVRE2ddc01310nam a2200289 a 450095201470000099900190014700300060016600500170017200800410018902000180023004000150024804100080026304400080027108200180027910000180029724501150031524600350043026000600046530000340052552002410055958600710080065000420087170000140091370000260092790100520095394200150