ssage inversé /cJonathan Bergmann, Aaron Sams, Marc-André Girard ; traduction et adaptation Marc-André Girard  aRepentigny :bÉditions Reynald Goulet,c2015  a152 pages :billustrations ;c22 cm1 aTechnologie de l'éducation  aSur la page de titre : ISTE  aDans ce second ouvrage, les pionniers de la classe inversée, Sams et Bergmann, vont au-delà de la simple inversion de la séquence pédagogique en se penchant sur les réels objectifs de maximisation du temps de classe avec les élèves. Plusieurs enseignants peuvent dispenser le contenu théorique de leur leçon à la maison à travers diverses lectures ou capsules vidéo, mais pour prétendre exploiter l'apprentissage inversé, les enseignants doivent adopter une pédagogie centrée sur l'élève. Les exemples sont concrets et inspirants et la traduction se veut une réelle adaptation à la culture francophone alors que quelques partages d'expérience proviennent d'enseignants reconnus pour leur utilisation de la classe inversée. [Memento]  pTraduction de:tFlipped learning. 6aEnseignement axé sur l'apprenant9295520 6aApprentissage par l'action912211  aSams, Aaron9209610  aTechnologie de l'éducation9267552  aAL (09-06-15)bAnnabel Labelle  cLIVRE2ddc  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2016-05-06g23.33l3m2o371.394 B499ap002136629r2023-08-02 00:00:00s2021-04-26yLIVRE  c388140d38814001575cam a2200337 a 0004465094CaQJC20250502123143.0ta130319t20132006fr a   g b    001 0 fre    a9782817803999  aBNFbfredCaQJC1 afreheng  afr05a510bA289r1 aAigner, Martin,d1942-10aRaisonnements divins :bquelques démonstrations mathématiques particulièrement élégantes /cMartin Aigner, Günter M. Ziegler ; traduit de l'anglais [d'après la 4e édition] par Nicolas Puech ; illustrations de Karl H. Hofmann.  a3e éd.  aParis :bSpringer,c2013, c2006.  ax, 308 p. :bill. ;c24 cm.  aIndex.  aRéf. bibliogr.  aRecueil de démonstrations mathématiques abordant différents domaines comme la théorie des nombres, l'analyse combinatoire ou la théorie des graphes. Propose aussi bien des résultats établis depuis longtemps que des théorèmes récemment démontrés, du postulat de Bertrand au théorème d'Ernst Witt, en passant par la décomposition des polyèdres selon David Hilbert. [Memento]  pTitre original:tProofs from the book. 6aMathématiques93974691 aZiegler, Günter M.1 aHofmann, Karl Heinrich  aAL (30-06-16)bAnnabel Labelle  cLIVRE2ddc  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2016-06-29g98.60l2m1o510 A289rp002141195r2024-06-17 00:00:00s2024-03-12yLIVRE  c388141d38814102348cam a22003257a 42847541CaQJC20250502123119.0070821s2006????dcua     b    001 0 eng?d  a0883856468  a9780883856468  aNJMbengcCaQJCdCaQJCdDLC0 aeng  axxu0 a519.27bP119m1 aPackel, Edward W.14aThe mathematics of games and gambling /cby Edward W. Packel.  a2nd ed.  aWashington, DC  :bMathematical Association of America,cc2006.  axiv, 175 p. :bill. ;c24 cm.1 aAnneli Lax new mathematical libraryv; 28  aIndex: p. 171-174.  aBibliogr.: p. 167-169.  aThe first edition of this book was reprinted eight times. This book introduces and develops some of the important and beautiful elementary mathematics needed for rational analysis of various gambling and game activities. Most of the standard casino games (roulette, blackjack, keno), some social games (backgammon, poker, bridge) and various other activities (state lotteries, horse racing, etc.) are treated in ways that bring out their mathematical aspects. The mathematics developed ranges from the predictable concepts of probability, expectation, and binomial coefficients to some less well-known ideas of elementary game theory. The second edition includes new material on: sports betting and the mathematics behind it; Game theory applied to bluffing in poker and related to the Texas Holdem phenomenon; The Nash equilibrium concept and its emergence in the popular culture; Internet links to games and to Java applets for practice and classroom use. The only formal mathematics background the reader needs is some facility with high school algebra. Game-related exercises are included at the end of most chapters for readers interested in working with and expanding ideas treated in the text. Solutions to some of the exercises appear at the end of the book. [Amazon] 6aJeux de hasard (Mathématiques)971987 0aAnneli Lax new mathematical libraryv; 28  aAL (20-05-16)bAnnabel Labelle  cLIVRE2ddc  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2016-05-20g60.74l0o519.27 P119mp002137219r2024-06-17 00:00:00yLIVRE  c388142d38814201749nam a2200373 a 0003887292CaQJC20250502123050.0120123s2010    fr a     b      1   fre    a9782848841144  aQMBNDbfre0 a793.74bC96203aLe cube :ble guide définitif du puzzle le plus vendu au monde : histoires secrètes, solutions, bonus mathématiques de l'édition française, le Rubik's Cube en France /c[sous la direction de] Jerry Slocum ; [avec la collaboration de] David Singmaster ... [et al.] ; [introdution d'Ernö Rubik] ; traduction et adaptation, Alain Zalmanski.3 iTitre de la couv.:aSecrets du cube :ble jeu hongrois qui a conquis le monde3 iTitre au dos:aSecrets du cube  aParis :bPole,c2010  a159 p. :bill. en coul. ;c24 cm.1 aBibliothèque Tangente  aIndex.  aGlossaire.  a"Le guide complet ; La lignée des casse-tête ; Les algorithmes de résolution" -- Couv.  aBibliogr.: p. 154.  aWebographie: p. 154.  aHistoire et guide de résolution du Rubik's Cube. Des spécialistes de l'histoire des jeux dispensent des méthodes et des conseils pour résoudre ses différentes versions. [Memento] 6aRubik, Cube92955211 aSlocum, Jerry1 aRubik, Ernö1 aSingmaster, David1 aZalmanski, Alain,d1935- 0aBibliothèque Tangente9113401  aAL (09-05-16)bAnnabel Labelle  cLIVRE2ddc  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2016-05-06g35.53l1o793.74 C962p002136645r2024-07-24 00:00:00s2023-11-08yLIVRE  c388143d38814301697nam a2200241 a 4500952012800000999001900128003000600147005001700153008004100170020001500211020001800226040001500244041000800259044000800267082001700275100002100292245004900313260005100362520098000413650002901393901001801422942001501440  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2016-06-08g12.71l2m1o519.3 B368mp002139075r2024-06-17 00:00:00s2016-10-28yLIVRE  c388144d388144CaQJC20180808135904.0160622b19892006xxu||||| |||| 00| 0 eng d  a0486449769  a9780486449760  aCaQJCbfre0 aeng  axxu0 a519.3bB368m1 aBeasley, John D.14aThe Mathematices of games /cJohn D. Beasley  aMineola, NY :bDover publications,c2006, 1989  a"Mind-exercising and thought-provoking."—New Scientist
If playing games is natural for humans, analyzing games is equally natural for mathematicians. Even the simplest of games involves the fundamentals of mathematics, such as figuring out the best move or the odds of a certain chance event. This entertaining and wide-ranging guide demonstrates how simple mathematical analysis can throw unexpected light on games of every type—games of chance, games of skill, games of chance and skill, and automatic games.
Just how random is a card shuffle or a throw of the dice? Is bluffing a valid poker strategy? How can you tell if a puzzle is unsolvable? How large a role does luck play in games like golf and soccer? This book examines each of these issues and many others, along with the general principles behind such classic puzzles as peg solitaire and Rubik's cube. Lucid, instructive, and full of surprises, it will fascinate mathematicians and gamesters alike. [Amazon] 6918951aThéorie des jeux  aAl (22-06-16)  cLIVRE2ddc01077cam a22003017i 450000100090000000300060000900500170001500800410003202000180007304000220009104100080011304400080012108200170012910000420014624501160018830000460030449000290035050000290037950400440040865000260045265000290047865000230050783000480053090100350057894200150061395201280062899900190075618632054CaQJC20250502145911.0150526t20152015flua     b    001 0 eng d  a9781482235432  aBTCTAbfrecCaQJC0 aeng  aflu0 a519.3bT238m1 aTaylor, David George,d1979-eauthor.14aThe mathematics of games :ban introduction to probability /cDavid G. Taylor, Roanoke College, Salem, VA, USA.  axxi, 404 pages :billustrations ;c24 cm.1 aTextbooks in mathematics  a"A Chapman & Hall book."  aComprend une bibliographie et un index. 6aProbabilités9397475 6aThéorie des jeux918951 6aStatistiques92091 0aTextbooks in mathematics (Boca Raton, Fla.)  aAL (13-06-16)bAnnabel Labelle  cLIVRE2ddc  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2016-06-08g55.91l3m1o519.3 T238mp002139067r2024-06-17 00:00:00s2022-12-20yLIVRE  c388145d38814501312nam a2200289 u 450000100090000000300060000900500170001500800410003202000180007304000150009104100080010604400070011408200150012110000300013624501050016626000390027130000410031052003470035165000250069865000500072365000250077370000280079890100350082694200150086195201270087699900190100342565087CaQJC20250502145547.0060321s2013||||fr ||||?|||||||||?|?fre||  a9782916340623  aCaQJCbfre0 afre