ours traditionnels rationnels. De nombreux cas pratiques de patients ayant pu venir à bout de leurs obsessions en se fixant des stratagèmes thérapeutiques planifiés sont présentés. -- [Renaud-Bray] 6aNévroses obsessionnelles965027 6aComportement compulsif94375 6aManie9400971 aPortelli, Claudette,eauteur1 aKoralnik, Nathalie,etraducteur  aAL (01-12-16)  cLIVRE  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2016-11-03g32.48l2m5o616.895 N224op002149004r2024-06-20 00:00:00s2018-09-17yLIVRE  c389698d38969800968nam a22003015i 450000100090000000300060000900500170001500800410003202000190007304000250009208200200011710000300013724500480016726400370021526400110025230000240026333600260028733700280031333800270034165000570036865000350042565100290046083000150048990100180050494200100052295201150053299900190064719188182CaQJC20161108143006.0160523s2016    fr            000 0 fre    a9782825146026   aDLCbengerdadCaQJC0 a844.914 bB656h1 aBlot, Jean,d1923-97726512aL'histoire du passé :bessai /cJean Blot. 1aParis :bL'Âge d'homme,c[2016] 4c©2016  a326 pages ;c21 cm.  atext2rdacontentbtxt  aunmediated2rdamediabn  avolume2rdacarrierbnc 69157963aHistoires pour enfantsxAspect psychologique 69299269aRessentimentxHistoire 6aÉgyptexHistoriographie 0aRue Férou  aAL (08-11-16)  cLIVRE  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2016-11-03g35.53l0o844.914 B656hp002148951r2024-08-09 00:00:00yLIVRE  c389704d38970401034nam a2200313 i 4500001001000000003000600010005001700016007000300033008004100036020001800077040002800095082001700123100004300140245005300183250001600236264004300252300002800295336002700323337003300350338002700383504006000410650002600470650003500496650002900531901001800560942001000578952011300588999001900701002373457CaQJC20161207145832.0ta160808s2016    quc      b    001 0 fre d  a9782896893560  aCaQMBNbfreerdadCaQJC0 a349.71bE54i1 aÉmond, André,d1956-eauteur929860110aIntroduc