avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aTraduction de: Nutrition for Canadians for dummies.  a"Manger sain et équilibré sans se casser la tête, déchiffrer les étiquettes de valeur nutritive, bien choisir son régime alimentaire, édition actualisée et complétée d'un livre 100 % adapté aux habitudes alimentaires des Québécois"--Couverture.  aComprend des références bibliographiques et un index. 6aNutrition920123 6aAlimentation958411 aCook, Doug,d1964-eauteur93103651 aMontpetit, Lindaeéditeur intellectuel9311186 0aPour les nuls (First (Firme))9313381  aAL (12-04-17)bAmélie Gauthier  cLIVRE  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2017-04-10g35.53l5m3o613.2 R584np002163749r2024-06-20 00:00:00s2024-03-01yLIVRE  c445035d44455201310cam a2200301 a 4500952014500000999001900145001001100164003000600175005001700181007000400198008004100202020001800243040002600261041000800287082001800295100001900313245011000332260003500442300002900477490002400506500001100530520031400541630002700855650006200882830003100944901001800975942001500993  00104070aCaQJCbCaQJCcLANAU.CGd2017-04-10g70.74l2o005.36 G536dp002163723r2023-05-30 00:00:00s2017-05-05v69.59w2017-04-10yLIVRE  c445041d4445580005221113CaQJC20190614090533.0ta 160218s2016    fr a   g      001 0 fre    a9782746099265  aBNFbfredSQTDdCaQJC0 afre0 a005.36bG536d1 aDauzon, Samuel10aGit :bmaîtrisez la gestion de vos versions : concepts, utilisation et cas pratiques /c[Samuel Dauzon].  aSaint-Herblain :bENI,c[2016]  a283 p. :bill. ;c21 cm.1 aEpsilon,x1960-3444  aIndex.  aConseils pratiques pour guider le lecteur dans l'installation et l'utilisation du logiciel de gestion de versions décentralisé Git, accompagné d'un focus sur la méthode git-flow. En complément, deux exemples de mise en situation permettent d'appréhender le logiciel de manière plus concrète. [Memento]64aGit (Logiciel)9311190 4aMaintenance de fichiers (Informatique)xLogiciels9311189 0aCollection Epsilon9311191  aAL (12-04-17)  cLIVRE2ddc02235nam a2200349 a 0004197769CaQJC20231026102733.0ta151027s2012||||xxua||||r||||01   e eng  a9781435458864  a1435458869  aDLCbfrecCaQMCLGdCaQJC0 aeng  axxu0 a794.81526bL566m 1 aLengyel, Eric931378810aMathematics for 3D game programming and computer graphics /cEric Lengyel.  a3rd ed.  aBoston, MA :bCourse Technology, Cengage Learning,c©2012  axviii, 545 p. :bill. (certaines en coul.), fig. ;c24 cm.  aIndex: p. 535-545.  aNotes bibliogr. au bas des p.  a
This updated third edition illustrates the mathematical concepts that a game developer needs to develop 3D computer graphics and game engines at the professional level. It starts at a fairly basic level in areas such as vector geometry and linear algebra, and then progresses to more advanced topics in 3D programming such as illumination and visibility determination. Particular attention is given to derivations of key results, ensuring that the reader is not forced to endure gaps in the theory. The book assumes a working knowledge of trigonometry and calculus, but also includes sections that review the important tools used from these disciplines, such as trigonometric identities, differential equations, and Taylor series. The third edition expands upon topics that include projections, shadows, physics, cloth simulation, and numerical methods. All of the illustrations have been updated, and the shader code has been updated to the latest high-level shading language specifications. [AbeBooks]


